  "variants": {
    "about": "A-4 (look pass M2): the dressing a mount KIND may take, so no row is one unit stamped twenty times. planDressing picks per bay with a seeded draw from the house id and bay index, never the same choice on two neighbouring bays, and may leave a mount empty (the 'empty' share). A CELL draws from at most `perCell` of a kind's files (rotated per cell by a seeded offset): every variant is a pool in its cell, and a cell holds at most 24/18/6 distinct files at LOD0/1/2 (section 8) -- so variety is BETWEEN neighbouring bays and BETWEEN cells, never all variants everywhere. A file placed at a mount takes the mount's axes. 'bench' mounts are the plinth's seat slots (two a window bay): a bench, a planter at ground (y 0, z +0.25) or nothing. Lamp variants are all glow members (MOONMERE_KIT.glows.members must list lamp_lantern and lamp_sconce). Vine variants spread at most +-1.0 m from the root, so they clear the bay's lamp; lemon_pot is the courts' and galleries' smaller tree.",
